# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, regardless of
# the user's core.autocrlf / core.eol setting. CRLF in a script's shebang
# breaks bash on Linux (`/bin/bash\r: no such file or directory`) — which
# is what happened when an SCP from a Windows working copy pushed a CRLF
# helper to the kiosk. Force LF in the repo so working copies on Windows
# also have LF and SCP / electron-builder ship LF unconditionally.
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf

# Same logic for systemd unit / desktop / sudoers fragments we ship as
# kiosk install assets — they're parsed line-by-line on Linux.
*.service    text eol=lf
*.desktop    text eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders: anything in resources/ is intended for a Linux
# runtime and should always be LF.
ElectronDock/resources/** text eol=lf
